Fix read.dcf() adding a duplicate column for every repeat of a field
whose name contains invalid UTF-8, which made the dcf target time out.

Since r90200 ("Always use UTF-8 for the DCF reader and writer"),
do_readDCF() (src/main/dcf.c) records a previously unseen field name in
repaired form (mkCharUTF8sub() turns "e\xfe" into "e<fe>") but keeps
matching later lines against the raw bytes.  The repaired name never
matches again, so each later occurrence of the field adds another
column, and each new column reallocates and copies the whole
field-by-record matrix.  read.dcf(all = TRUE) is unaffected, since its
R code repairs every line first.  On an 11 KB input the default path
built a 388 x 535 matrix where all = TRUE gives 388 x 20, taking 0.85 s
on a release build and over a minute under ASan:

    ==1570== ERROR: libFuzzer: timeout after 61 seconds
        #4 STRING_ELT              src/main/memory.c:4132
        #5 do_readDCF              src/main/dcf.c:301
        #6 bcEval_loop             src/main/eval.c:8150
       ...
       #24 LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput  harnesses/dcf.c:56

Repair the whole line as soon as it is read, as the all = TRUE code
does, so stored field names and later lines use the same bytes.  The
repaired copy comes from R_alloc() with exactly strlen + 1 bytes, so
the two error paths that cut the line at 20 bytes for the message now
check its length first.

Found by fuzzing R with libFuzzer + AddressSanitizer (OSS-Fuzz dcf
target, testcase 5506677886222336).  The regression is in R-devel only
(r90200 and later); R 4.6.1 is not affected.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #349; R Bugzilla bug 19194
(attachment 3881).  The upstream patch also adds a regression test to tests/reg-tests-1e.R,
left out here so this carry patch does not go stale with that file.
The hunks are made against a tree with patch 0015 applied, which also
changes do_readDCF().  Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk
(ossfuzz.sh will report it as already-applied in the meantime, which is
harmless).

diff --git a/src/main/dcf.c b/src/main/dcf.c
index 47faa15c9b..29b994f24a 100644
--- a/src/main/dcf.c
+++ b/src/main/dcf.c
@@ -176,6 +176,13 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_readDCF(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
     void *vmax = vmaxget();
     char buf0[MAXELTSIZE];
     while((line = Rconn_getline2(con, buf0, MAXELTSIZE))) {
+	/* Repair invalid UTF-8 in the whole line before matching, as the
+	   all = TRUE R code does: a new field name is recorded repaired, so
+	   matching its later occurrences against the raw bytes would fail
+	   and add a duplicate column for each.  The repaired copy comes from
+	   R_alloc() and may be shorter than 21 bytes. */
+	if(!utf8Valid(line))
+	    line = (char *) reEnc3(line, "UTF-8", "UTF-8", 1);
 	if(strlen(line) == 0 ||
 	   tre_regexecb(&blankline, line, 0, 0, 0) == 0) {
 	    /* A blank line.  The first one after a record ends a new
@@ -204,7 +211,8 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_readDCF(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 		/* A continuation line: wrong if at the beginning of a
 		   record. */
 		if((lastm == -1) && !field_skip) {
-		    line[20] = '\0';
+		    if(strlen(line) > 20)
+			line[20] = '\0';
 		    error(_("Found continuation line starting '%s ...' at begin of record."),
 			  line);
 		}
@@ -342,7 +350,8 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_readDCF(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 		    }
 		} else {
 		    /* Must be a regular line with no tag ... */
-		    line[20] = '\0';
+		    if(strlen(line) > 20)
+			line[20] = '\0';
 		    error(_("Line starting '%s ...' is malformed!"), line);
 		}
 	    }
